---
# One terse line per decision; the full rationale for each - measurements, failed
# experiments, reproduction steps - lives in the commit that made it (git log -S
# the check name) and its PR. Sorted like the list below: by check name, ignoring
# the leading '-'.
#
# The CppCoreGuidelines bounds/type-safety profile is triaged per check, not off
# as a group: this library IS the container/hash layer those checks assume code
# sits above, so each one is judged on where its findings actually land.
#   ON  avoid-unchecked-container-access (2026-08-16). No ExcludeClasses: that
#       option misses aliases and absl's inherited operator[], so exemptions live
#       in the code as ranged NOLINTs where they can be seen. It found a real bug.
#   ON  pro-type-union-access, pro-bounds-constant-array-index. 890 findings, but
#       798 sit in four types whose union IS their storage (OptionalDataOrRef,
#       LimitedVector, LimitedOrdered, NoDestruct) plus the kernels - all ranged
#       NOLINT blocks, no code changed.
#   OFF pro-bounds-pointer-arithmetic. Our iterators are raw pointers, so it fires
#       on `it + n` - ordinary random-access iterator use, at every CALLER. A
#       recurring tax on correct code, not a defect it can find.
#   OFF pro-bounds-array-to-pointer-decay (= hicpp-no-array-decay). Fires wherever
#       a string literal reaches generic code: StrAppend(&m, fwd<T>(arg)), the
#       stream operators, forwarding ctors. Suppressing that is noise, not safety.
#
# abseil-unchecked-statusor-access: clang-tidy 22.1.8 SEGFAULTS in its dataflow on
#   this code; re-test on a future LLVM.
# bugprone-crtp-constructor-accessibility: its advice was tried - a private ctor
#   makes Extend types non-aggregates, breaking `{.a = ...}` construction.
# bugprone-easily-swappable-parameters: flags adjacent same-type params on pure
#   heuristic. TODO(helly25): re-enable once the flagged interfaces are revisited.
# bugprone-random-generator-seed (+ cert-msc32-c, cert-msc51-cpp): constant seeds
#   are deliberate - tests and benchmarks must reproduce.
# bugprone-std-namespace-modification: our `namespace std` blocks are sanctioned
#   specialisations (std::hash, structured bindings), not additions.
# cert-dcl50-cpp (+ modernize-avoid-variadic-functions): variadic visitors are the
#   signature __builtin_dump_struct dictates; the reflection core cannot avoid them.
# cppcoreguidelines-macro-usage: the flagged macros feed the PREPROCESSOR (#if),
#   where constexpr does not exist.
# cppcoreguidelines-avoid-magic-numbers (+ readability-magic-numbers, aliases):
#   fire on test expectations and the numeric tables that ARE the subject.
# hicpp-*: off as a module, then two re-enabled. 27 of its 31 checks are ALIASES
#   of checks we already run under their canonical names - verified: with both
#   enabled a single diagnostic names both, e.g. `[cppcoreguidelines-pro-bounds-
#   array-to-pointer-decay,hicpp-no-array-decay]`. Aliases add no coverage, only
#   a second name and a second place to keep in sync. Of the 4 that are unique:
#   - hicpp-exception-baseclass: ON. This repo does not use exceptions - the one
#     path that can throw is MBO_CONFIG_REQUIRE under `kRequireThrows`, and it
#     throws std::runtime_error. The check keeps it that way if that ever grows.
#   - hicpp-multiway-paths-covered: ON. Wants every switch/if-else chain to cover
#     its paths (default/else), which is a real bug class, not a style rule.
#   - hicpp-signed-bitwise: OFF. Parity masks over signed ptrdiff_t in the Myers
#     diff; diagonals run negative, the signedness is the algorithm's.
#   - hicpp-no-assembler: OFF. No inline asm here; the check only adds noise if
#     a portability-driven intrinsic ever needs it.
# llvm-header-guard: STYLE_CPP mandates {PATH}_{FILE}_; the header-guards hook
#   enforces what this check structurally cannot.
# llvm-prefer-static-over-anonymous-namespace: anonymous namespaces are the
#   convention here, not per-function static.
# misc-include-cleaner: fights the umbrella headers by demanding includes of
#   internal/ headers; IWYU proper is the tool if hygiene is ever wanted.
# misc-no-recursion: the flagged code is recursive by design (Stringify walks,
#   parser descent); an explicit stack would be longer and less clear.
# misc-use-internal-linkage: its only fix is `static` (against STYLE_CPP), and on
#   header-declared functions that breaks the build via -Wunused-function.
# readability-inconsistent-ifelse-braces: 20/25 findings point INTO the
#   MBO_*_RETURN macros' call sites, unfixable there; clang-format's InsertBraces
#   already braces real bodies.
# readability-redundant-parentheses: its fix deletes the __builtin_dump_struct
#   callee (a clang-tidy bug around the builtin's own expansion), corrupting the
#   reflection machinery.
# readability-use-concise-preprocessor-directives: the #ifdef rewrite cannot apply
#   to the compound conditions next door, making neighbours less consistent.
#
# Kept, with options below: cppcoreguidelines-rvalue-reference-param-not-moved
# uses IgnoreNonDeducedTemplateTypes (a class template's Container&& is a real
# rvalue ref that may instantiate as T&, where std::forward is correct);
# readability-identifier-naming exempts {PATH}_{FILE}_ guard macros its UPPER_CASE
# splitter can never accept (the header-guards hook owns that rule).
#
# Comments must stay OUTSIDE the folded scalar below: text inside it is content,
# parsed as check globs.
Checks: >
  *,
  abseil-*,
  -abseil-unchecked-statusor-access,
  -altera-*,
  -boost-*,
  bugprone-*,
  -bugprone-crtp-constructor-accessibility,
  -bugprone-easily-swappable-parameters,
  -bugprone-exception-escape,
  -bugprone-random-generator-seed,
  -bugprone-std-namespace-modification,
  -cert-dcl50-cpp,
  -cert-err58-cpp,
  -cert-msc32-c,
  -cert-msc51-cpp,
  clang*,
  clang-analyzer-*,
  clang-diagnostic-*,
  cppcoreguidelines-*,
  -cppcoreguidelines-pro-bounds-array-to-pointer-decay,
  -cppcoreguidelines-pro-bounds-pointer-arithmetic,
  -cppcoreguidelines-avoid-const-or-ref-data-members,
  -cppcoreguidelines-avoid-magic-numbers,
  -cppcoreguidelines-macro-usage,
  -fuchsia*,
  google-*,
  -google-build-using-namespace,
  -hicpp-*,
  hicpp-exception-baseclass,
  hicpp-multiway-paths-covered,
  -llvm-else-after-return,
  -llvm-header-guard,
  -llvm-include-order,
  -llvm-prefer-static-over-anonymous-namespace,
  -llvmlibc-*,
  misc-*,
  -misc-include-cleaner,
  -misc-no-recursion,
  -misc-use-internal-linkage,
  modernize-*,
  -modernize-avoid-variadic-functions,
  -modernize-use-nodiscard,
  -modernize-use-std-format,
  -modernize-use-trailing-return-type,
  performance-*,
  -performance-enum-size,
  portability-*,
  readability-*,
  -readability-avoid-nested-conditional-operator,
  -readability-else-after-return,
  -readability-inconsistent-ifelse-braces,
  -readability-magic-numbers,
  -readability-redundant-inline-specifier,
  -readability-redundant-parentheses,
  -readability-use-concise-preprocessor-directives,

# A check-name glob, not a bool: the former `true` matched no check, so findings
# never escalated to a non-zero exit.
WarningsAsErrors: '*'
# Generated data tables (`*.inc`) are not hand-edited: any finding in one has to
# be fixed in the generator that emits it, so reporting it at the generated file
# is noise. `hash_test_vectors.inc` is the case in point - it is produced by
# //mbo/hash:hash_test_vectors_gen and #included by hash_test.cc.
ExcludeHeaderFilterRegex: '.*\.inc$'
FormatStyle:       '.clang-format'
CheckOptions:
  - key:             bugprone-signed-char-misuse.CharTypedefsToIgnore
    value:           'int8_t'
  - key:             google-readability-braces-around-statements.ShortStatementLines
    value:           '1'
  - key:             google-readability-function-size.StatementThreshold
    value:           '800'
  - key:             google-readability-namespace-comments.ShortNamespaceLines
    value:           '25'
  - key:             google-readability-namespace-comments.SpacesBeforeComments
    value:           '2'
  - key:             misc-non-private-member-variables-in-classes.IgnoreClassesWithAllMemberVariablesBeingPublic
    value:           '1'
  - key:             modernize-loop-convert.MaxCopySize
    value:           '16'
  - key:             modernize-loop-convert.MinConfidence
    value:           reasonable
  - key:             modernize-loop-convert.NamingStyle
    value:           CamelCase
  - key:             modernize-pass-by-value.IncludeStyle
    value:           llvm
  - key:             modernize-replace-auto-ptr.IncludeStyle
    value:           llvm
  - key:             modernize-use-default-member-init.UseAssignment
    value:           '1'
  - key:             modernize-use-emplace.IgnoreImplicitConstructors
    value:           '1'
  - key:             modernize-use-nullptr.NullMacros
    value:           'NULL'
  - key:             performance-unnecessary-value-param.AllowedTypes
    value:           'absl::Status;absl::StatusOr;mbo::types::ConstStrongId.*;mbo::types::ConstStrongOrdinal.*;mbo::types::StrongOrdinal.*;std::string_view'
  - key:             cppcoreguidelines-rvalue-reference-param-not-moved.IgnoreNonDeducedTemplateTypes
    value:           '1'
  - key:             readability-implicit-bool-conversion.AllowIntegerConditions
    value:           '1'
  - key:             readability-implicit-bool-conversion.AllowPointerConditions
    value:           '1'
  - key:             readability-function-cognitive-complexity.Threshold
    value:           '30'
  - key:             readability-braces-around-statements.ShortStatementLines
    value:           '1'
  - key:             readability-identifier-length.IgnoredLoopCounterNames
    value:           'i|it|n'
  - key:             readability-identifier-length.IgnoredParameterNames
    value:           'os|v'
  - key:             readability-identifier-length.IgnoredVariableNames
    value:           'os|v|it|_'
  - key:             cppcoreguidelines-non-private-member-variables-in-classes.IgnoreClassesWithAllMemberVariablesBeingPublic
    value:           '1'
  - key:             readability-identifier-naming.ClassCase
    value:           CamelCase
  - key:             readability-identifier-naming.ClassMemberCase
    value:           lower_case
  - key:             readability-identifier-naming.ConstexprVariableCase
    value:           CamelCase
  - key:             readability-identifier-naming.ConstexprVariablePrefix
    value:           k
  - key:             readability-identifier-naming.EnumCase
    value:           CamelCase
  - key:             readability-identifier-naming.EnumConstantCase
    value:           CamelCase
  - key:             readability-identifier-naming.EnumConstantPrefix
    value:           k
  - key:             readability-identifier-naming.FunctionCase
    value:           CamelCase
  - key:             readability-identifier-naming.GlobalConstantCase
    value:           CamelCase
  - key:             readability-identifier-naming.GlobalConstantPrefix
    value:           k
  - key:             readability-identifier-naming.StaticConstantCase
    value:           CamelCase
  - key:             readability-identifier-naming.StaticConstantPrefix
    value:           k
  - key:             readability-identifier-naming.StaticVariableCase
    value:           lower_case
  - key:             readability-identifier-naming.MacroDefinitionCase
    value:           UPPER_CASE
  - key:             readability-identifier-naming.MacroDefinitionIgnoredRegexp
    value:           '^[A-Z][A-Z0-9]*(_[A-Z0-9]+)*_$'
  - key:             readability-identifier-naming.MemberCase
    value:           lower_case
  - key:             readability-identifier-naming.PrivateMemberSuffix
    value:           _
  - key:             readability-identifier-naming.PublicMemberSuffix
    value:           ''
  - key:             readability-identifier-naming.NamespaceCase
    value:           lower_case
  - key:             readability-identifier-naming.ParameterCase
    value:           lower_case
  - key:             readability-identifier-naming.TypeAliasCase
    value:           CamelCase
  - key:             readability-identifier-naming.TypedefCase
    value:           CamelCase
  - key:             readability-identifier-naming.VariableCase
    value:           lower_case
  - key:             readability-identifier-naming.IgnoreMainLikeFunctions
    value:           1
  # The C++ standard's container, iterator, allocator and functor requirements
  # MANDATE these member type names, spelled exactly like this. A type that wants
  # to satisfy them - and thus work with the standard algorithms, ranges, and
  # anything else that asks a container for its `value_type` - has no choice about
  # the spelling, so CamelCase is not an option. Everything else still has to be
  # CamelCase.
  - key:             readability-identifier-naming.TypeAliasIgnoredRegexp
    value:           '^(type|value_type|size_type|difference_type|reference|const_reference|pointer|const_pointer|iterator|const_iterator|reverse_iterator|const_reverse_iterator|iterator_category|iterator_concept|allocator_type|key_type|mapped_type|key_compare|value_compare|key_equal|hasher|element_type|traits_type|char_type|int_type|pos_type|off_type|state_type|result_type|argument_type|first_argument_type|second_argument_type|is_transparent)$'
  - key:             readability-identifier-naming.TypedefIgnoredRegexp
    value:           '^(type|value_type|size_type|difference_type|reference|const_reference|pointer|const_pointer|iterator|const_iterator|reverse_iterator|const_reverse_iterator|iterator_category|iterator_concept|allocator_type|key_type|mapped_type|key_compare|value_compare|key_equal|hasher|element_type|traits_type|char_type|int_type|pos_type|off_type|state_type|result_type|argument_type|first_argument_type|second_argument_type|is_transparent)$'
  - key:             readability-identifier-naming.ClassIgnoredRegexp
    value:           'type'
  - key:             readability-identifier-naming.ConstexprVariableIgnoredRegexp
    value:           'value|index|.*[a-z]V'
...
